// Same policy as 1155 (`previous within 1h Login`). The ONLY difference from
// 1155 is the event schema: here the `callerPrincipal` pin is PARTIAL (on
// `request` only), so it is not universal and partitioning is NOT active — the
// leaf keeps global-trace semantics. On the shared trace 1155 permits (foreign
// event excluded); this bundle must DENY (foreign event is the global
// `previous`). The divergence is caused by the partial vs universal pin alone.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    previous within 1h Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{ input.user: context.input.user }
};
